---
import BasicLayout from '@/layouts/BasicLayout.astro';
---

<BasicLayout title="Privacy Policy | Encode Edge" description="Our privacy policy explains how we handle information collected on Encode Edge.">
  <div class="mb-8 border-b pb-6">
    <span class="woords_tag_small mb-3">Legal</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl text-foreground tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground mt-2">Last updated: September 2026</p>
  </div>

  <h2>1. Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Encode Edge ("we", "our", or "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting the personal information you share with us. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect, how we use it, and your choices regarding your data.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>
  <p>
    We collect minimal information necessary to deliver educational tutorials, interactive notebooks, and newsletter subscriptions:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Newsletter Subscriptions:</strong> When you subscribe to our newsletter, we collect your email address.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact Forms:</strong> When you send a message through our contact form, we collect your name, email, and inquiry.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage & Analytics:</strong> We use privacy-conscious analytics tools (with consent management) to monitor aggregated traffic patterns and tutorial readership.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Cookies & Consent</h2>
  <p>
    We respect your cookie preferences. You can update or withdraw your consent for analytics and preference cookies at any time using our cookie settings dialog.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We may partner with trusted infrastructure providers (such as hosting and email delivery services) that adhere to strict data protection standards.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact Us</h2>
  <p>
    If you have any questions or concerns about this policy, please reach out via our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</BasicLayout>

